        <p>Mr. Gladstone looked in excellent health and spirits in the House of Commons on Monday. He alternately chatted and laughed with Sir William Harcourt on the right, and the boyish Under-Secretary for Foreign Affairs Sir Edward Grey, on the left. His vivacity and alert- ness were the theme of general and admiring comment, showing as they did that his recent indisposition had left no perceptible ill effects in its train.</p>
