      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1893-03-25_WidnesExaminer_art0042" n="art0042">
        <head>" GETTIN' W[CKERT."</head>
        <p>" GETTIN' W[CKERT."</p>
        <p>Onst on a time, two buzzum chums Seet eaut to hey a spree; Surnwheer i'th' rep,ion o' Lone Yed, On th' road to Bedford-Leigh. (The owdest mon i' Colborne BA He heerd it wen a b'y ; An' surely wi' one foote i'th' grave, Ile wudn't tell a lie.) One on urn wur a Carter bold, Ez ever play'd a" lark ;" Tho' Ise wur one o'th' deaubtful sort, To travel wi' "i'th' dark." His seet wur bad, he allus sed, . Wenever owt went wrung; Although it man be owned, alas I His yed wur rayther strung ! His matey kept a Public Heause, Weel noted fer good cheer ; An' if yo wanted deawnreet fun, Yo'd allus get it theer. Well, off thay went, on frolic bent, Exparience to buy; Till th' " Bull" wur reyched, wen th carter sett His throat wur gettin' dry. Reaund after reaund went rowlin' deawn, Till midneet welly coom ; Wen, like that Ilea wi' th' candle brunt, " Ther pleasure proved ther doom Fer wen thay geet ereawt i'th' road, It wur ez dark ez pitch ; An' th' Host, he tumbled neck an' crop, Reet in a five-foote ditch ! • Yo shud ha' heerd that joker sheaut It 0' Colborne Sage towd true— But s.w he sad war," Cain, owd Ger owt o' me an' poo ! " Poo like the dale, er else, by G yow I My eend is gettin' near But th' lonlert, he wer clabblet up, He cudn't shift fer fear! At lung length, a policeman coo, An' made his bull's eye flash ; Wen laughin', he to th' Caterer said— "Well, heaw dost like thi wash ?" " Tak' howd, an'gie thysel a jerk, An' don't make such a din ; Theaur't only frickent, lad, not hurt— Theaur't only just NOW Inn!" So, safely landed, they went worn, Like quickly sober'd men ; An' never, till ther deein' day, Went on the spree agen</p>
        <p>Tun o' PEGS. Rose Bonk, March 23rd, 1893,</p>
      </div>
