rous liberality, which h c%ad enabit,,vec promoters of that social evening to provide. s) ex ,`, lg. a repast and pleasing entertain4l.' spnYl ent. There Cnet4 of no doubt that the police if they bad thas to the law abiding public would render their the best of their ability.—lnspeetor Cooper al .:"1. ported the motion which WAS carried by 0n . anclarri;, A vote of thanks was accorded to the Chairman ollo; ;:nd motion of Mr. Coventry. seconded by p.s. woo „gal supported by P.S. Cosling.—The company then ent . CO in a variety of amusing games, and su bseque%l down to an excellent supper, and the proceoding c eluded about one o'clock. -</p>
