        <p>COUNTY OF CHESTER. TO CARTERS, FARMERS, AND TEAM OWNERS. PERSONS desirous of TENDERING for CARTING MACADAM and other Materials for the Main Roads for the year ending 31st March, 1894. can obtain Forms of Tender and particulars Of Material to he carted, at this Office, on and after Monday, the 20th inst., betweea 10 a.tn. and 4 p.m., and on Saturday between 10 a.m. and 1 p.m. Tenders to be endorsed "Tender for Carting" to he delivered at this Office on or before Saturday, the 15th April, 1893. The Main Roads Committee of the County Council do not bind themselves to accept the lowest or any Tender. STANHOPE BULL, County Surveyor. County Surveyor's Office, Northgate Chambers, Chester, 18th March, 1893.</p>
        <p>NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN, that the next GEN- ERAL QUARTER SESSIONS ,f the Peace for the COUNTY OF CHESTER will be opened at the COURT HOUSE, NETHER KNUT,FORD, in and for the said County, on MONDAY, the 3rd day of April next, at half- past Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon, but in consequence of that day being a Bank Holiday the business of the Court will be adjourned to the following day at the same time, when the Grand Jury will be empannelled. The hearing of the Appeals arising within the Hundreds of Bucklow, Macclesfield and Northwich, forming the Knutsford District, and the trials of all prisoners corn- tnitted from such Hundreds, will take ph ce at such Sessions. The Grand and Petty Juries for the Knutsford District must be in attendance at the Court House, Knutsford, on TUESDAY, the 4th day of April next, at Half-past Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon. THE Court will be adjourned to the Castle of Chester, on THURSDAY, the 6th day of April next, at Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon. The hearing of all Aopeals arising within the Hundreds of Broxton, Eddisbury, Nantwich and Wirral, forming the Chester District, and the trials of all prisoners committed from the last-men- tioned Hnndreds will take place at such adjourned Ses- sions. 'The Grand and Petty Jurirs for the Chester District must be in attendance at the Castle of Chester, at the opening of the Court on THURSDAY, the 6th day of April next, at Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon. REGINALD POTTS. Clerk of the Peace for the County of Chester. r Chester, 13th March, 1893.</p>
