        <p>DR. J. COLLIS BROWNE'S CHLORODYNE• THE ORIGINAL AND ONLY GENUINE. LORODYNE is admitted by the Profession to be the most wonderful and valuable remedy ever dis- covered. CII.LORODYNE is the best remedy known for Coughs, Consumption, Bronchitis, and Asthma. CBLORODYNE effectually checks and arrests those too often fatal diseases.—Diptheria, Fever, Cromp, Ague. CIILORODYNE acts like a charm in Diarrhcea, and is the only specific in Cholera and Dysentry. CHLORODYNE effectually cuts short all attacks of Epilepsy, Hysteria, Palpitation, and Spasms. 011LORODYNE is the only palliative in Neural- gia, Rheumatism, Gout, Cancer, Toothache, Meningitis, ' Bco. From Dr. B. J. BOULTON &amp; Co., Horncastle. We have made pretty extensive use of Chlorodyne in our practice lately, and look upon it as an excellent direct z'.eda- tive and Anti- spasmodic. It seems to allay pain and irrita- tion in whatever organ, and from whatever cause. It induces a feeling of comfort and quietude not obtainable by any other remedy. and it seems to possess this great advan- age over all other Sedatives ; that it leaves no unpleasant after effects. " Earl Russell communicated to the College of Physicians that he received a despatch from her Majesty's Consul at Manilla, to the effect that Cholera kad been raging fearfully and that the ONLY remedy of any s.rvice was CHLORO- DYNE."—see Lancet , let December, 1864. CAUTION.—BEWARE OF PIRACY AND IMIT- ATIONS. CAUTION.—Vice Chancellor Sir W. PAGE WOOD stated that Dr. J. CoLVte BROWNE. was, undoubtedly, the inventor of CHLORODYNE " and that the story of the defendant FREE- MAN, was deliberately untrue, which he regretted to 5a3 uad been sworn to.—See Times, 13th Joly ,1864, Sold in bottles at Is. 10., 2s. 9d., and 4s. 6d. None Is genuine without the words "Dll. J. COLLIS BROWNE'S CHLORODYNE "on the Government Stamp. Overwhelm. hig Medical testimony accompanies each battle. BOLE MANUFACTURERS.—J• T. DAVENPORT, 33, Great Russell. st., Bloomsbury. London.</p>
